Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: drop meaningless IRQF_ONESHOT flag

The driver passes a NULL thread function, for which IRQF_ONESHOT is
a no-op, and __setup_irq() warns about exactly this combination.
Drop the flag; behavior is unchanged.
---
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
@@ -431,7 +431,7 @@ static int eip93_crypto_probe(struct pla
 		return eip93->irq;
 
 	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(eip93->dev, eip93->irq, eip93_irq_handler,
-					NULL, IRQF_ONESHOT,
+					NULL, 0,
 					dev_name(eip93->dev), eip93);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
